506:* ''Integrity owed: the floor's trust chain'' (`W14`, `W15`, `W16`: the signed floor card, the pin's causal position, carry-floor convergence). Its witness: a rotation-and-carry storm that accepts no stale pin and converges the same way on every carrier.
512:* `W14` The floor card a banner carries in its `#floor=` link reads unsigned, on origin trust; a signed card stays owed. The floor read by release (`W26` slice 4) adds one rung and closes nothing here: a browser holding the Nexus AID verifies the epoch lineage, the head release and the floor bytes itself (`browser-floor-read`), anchored to the AID alone, since the genesis epoch re-derives it. The lineage rides the release record and the porch answer, never the card (a card holds 4096 characters, and the lineage self-certifies); that carrier changes nothing about trust, because the AID that anchors it comes from the card or the genesis CID the reader already pins and never from the answer, and an answer self-consistent for another AID refuses (`floor-answer.test`). The AID itself still rides the same-origin trust line, and nothing proves the card's freshness: the signed card (`W14`), the pin's causal position (`W15`) and the carry-floor convergence (`W16`) stay owed for anchoring the AID and the card. W.
513:* `W15` A floor pin statement carries no causal position, and `hearthPinIndex` files first-wins, so a rotated floor key re-files only on restart (`admit-gate-pin.ts`, `place-floor-pin.ts`). W.
514:* `W16` Two-vault carry: the carry partials land no floor pin, so a cofounded Nexus carries no herm yet (`nexus-contract.ts`). W.
515:* `W26` The system wikis release and every other wiki reads the floor (#/rulings, 2026-10-16). Slice 1 stands (PR #49): genesis carries the first floor, its manifest and the `lares` and `lararium` snapshots by CID, and `@oracle` reads that floor by CID. Slice 2 stands (PR #52): each vessel's system, crossroads and realm pointers rest in its own `@catalog`, and nothing writes the shared `@oracle` after genesis (`oracle-doc-no-writer.test.ts`). Slice 3 stands (lane `--w26-floor-3`): the founding lands the counted 1-of-1 Kahu admission for persona zero's group (`landFoundingAdmission`) and registers `lares` and `lararium` as realm bags of the hearth's realm under persona zero's per-Nexus key (`landKahuRealm`); `kahuCabalCanonAccess` has its production caller (`kahuReachSourceOf`); the keel mounts only what the realm names, the registered bag set and the `bags/` mirrors follow, and no catalog row names a system bag. Slice 6 stands: one predicate (`requireKahuReach`) guards the residency reactor, meme put and delete, draft placement and a realm steward's write, and the keyholder island's verifier carries it for `--in-wiki` verbs. Slice 4 stands: the release (`floor-release`: body, CID, steward seal by a seated Kahu key, the cabal's high-impact approval of the manifest's exact bytes, the charter's epoch lineage), the chain fold, `lares nexus release`, the porch (`GET /floor/<Nexus AID>`, `/cas/<cid>` for the head's blobs), the browser's verified read, and the flow map's own `flow-pointer` domain in place of the retired `oracle-pointer`. The build runs six slices in order, under the architecture of #/rulings (2026-10-18), its shape and evidence at <<~ loulou "lar:///ha.ka.ba/lares/docs/pono/w26-floor-lane">>: (1) the floor manifest and its read-face, genesis baking the first floor; (2) each vessel's pointers leave the shared document for its bootstrap, re-cutting `W21`; (3) the Kahu realm holds the live system documents, and a one-seat founding lands its 1-of-1 Kahu admission; (4) the release answer on the crossroads, folding `P8`; (5) the accept act per (face, Nexus), which follows Wave C's face context since its accepted floor rests as a face's D row; (6) reach into system canon refuses every hand outside the cabal. OWED: a browser Kahu hand rides Wave C's face context (the browser composes no board reader and reads as a stranger, fail closed); a sibling device of a seat-holding face reads the floor until that context carries the charter and the board to it; the carriage `canon` names (`device-admit.ts` `admitCanonDocs`, the browser's `hearth-canon`) read rows nothing writes now, and retire with `W21`'s rest. W.
524:* `W28` The sealed channel's frame layout (`gate-exchange.ts` `GATE_FRAME`, tags `0x01` to `0x13`) still reads "provisional", owned by no row, while both operators' vessels speak it on every dial (`face-dial.ts`, `face-gate.ts`). It freezes before the bake: the tag table, the fragment bound and the verdict length, with a reserved-tag rule so a later frame adds a tag and moves none. Pairs with the `W10` research pair, since both move the dial's bytes once. W.
536:* ''Integrity owed: the bake's cross-product'' (`X0`, touching `K15` step 6, `W26`, `G37`). Its witness: one matrix over the pre-bake and post-bake artifacts, every old CID refused after the bake and a fresh two-of-two founding standing, rather than greens read row by row.
