581:* `P18` The shared-canon read consults `kahuCabalCanonAccess`, admission AND sentinel membership; until it does, a removed group keeps its Keyhive sentinel capability at every reader but that one (`boot-daemon-keyhive`). Both vessels' daemon payloads (`open-node-vessel.ts`, `open-browser-vessel.ts`) carry the group and sentinel ids alone, so each composition threads the Nexus AID, the seated roster and the carriage board into the read together; a node-only gate leaves the browser reader open. P.
