604:* `X0b` The idempotent-by-intent pass, after the founding bake, paralleling the isomorphic-by-intent law (operator, 2026-10-19): a replay, a reboot and a retry land nothing new. Every row names itself by its content or its causal id, never a clock or a counter; every write reads first-writer-wins or merges by its CRDT; every boot reads as a function of its stores; and every multi-step act either completes or re-enters to the same end. Its instrument: N boots, each Archive replayed twice, each verb retried, and the second pass of each adds no head and no row. Each finding before the bake cures as its own bug; its instrument runs once before the bake as a census beside `G37`, so a finding that renames a persisted row lands inside the bake, and this pass sweeps what remains. X.
