/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/persona-policy.mem:42:''A face names WHO ANSWERS for an act'' — one blame-bearer per act; correlation stays secondary. The ruling calls for recording outgoing and incoming faces locally with causal position and rebind/re-dial results, closing the switching session's Nexus links, then re-dialing as the incoming face (#/the-session: the switch belongs to ONE session and touches no other). The recorded switch act stands ruled, unbuilt: the code as it stands keeps ONE vessel-wide selector and resolves one worn face at vessel boot, so a switch takes a restart until that act lands. A session wears ONE face at a time, either a private face alone or paired with its public Handle; a personal Handle never rides without its owning face.
