/home/joshu/Synthetic-Dream-Machine/bags/lares/ha.ka.ba/lares/api/pono/kapae.mem:256:''The doors.'' `lares edge kapae` and `un-kapae` act by an edge id, by `--member` with `--realm`, or by `--device`; `--quorum` signs with the seats this vessel holds of the charter the realm stands under. On a realm's board the holder signs with the worn face's key at that Nexus, and `--as` names a fleet root on a fleet's board alone. `lares cabal face`, `vouch`, `feed` and `join` act as the worn face's key at the realm's Nexus, and `--nexus` names that Nexus at a vessel's first act in a realm; the vessel's edge ledger keeps the realm's Nexus (`noteRealm`, `ledgerRealmNexus`), and every door and reader takes the realm's charter through it (`edge-board`). A crossing names each shadow it met: over a vouch, over a voucher, over the applicant. A seal roll anchors every realm edge board whose quorum acts the rolling vessel keeps, of a realm standing under the Nexus that rolls. `lares edge settle` answers, on the key side, each raise this vessel counts on its fleet's board, and a standing vessel runs the same three steps by itself: each fold of its fleet's edge board sets off one settle, with no timer and no person (`seat-settle`). The vessel's main thread reads the fold, places the island's `seat-duties` verb and awaits its answer on the daemon's document, then keeps the signed rolls in its own ledger. A raise whose seat it saw leave owes nothing at any later fold; one answered with no revoke authority keeps its roll and gets tried again at the next fold. The settle runs on an unlocked vessel that holds the root of the fleet its own device edge names, as the command does, and a vessel under a shadow of its own places nothing. With `--quorum --partial` a vessel that holds fewer seats than an act takes signs its part, and `lares edge cosign` adds another vessel's seats and lands the act once it counts.
